WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.960
The "Wonder Woman" series is&nbsp;
reportedly no more – or at least,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.360
it's not going to happen the&nbsp;
way the director meant it to.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.620
"You should be ashamed."

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.220
"My apologies."

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:08.858
"You should be ashamed."

00:00:08.858 --> 00:00:09.386
"Diana."

00:00:09.386 --> 00:00:13.140
In the wake of such critical&nbsp;
failures as "Batman v. Superman:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:18.540
Dawn of Justice" and "Suicide Squad," fans&nbsp;
of DC started to rapidly lose faith in Warner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:23.160
Bros. Despite being only a few installments&nbsp;
into what was then the DC Extended Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:28.440
the studio had already demonstrated a worrisome&nbsp;
inability to keep their film quality consistent.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:33.780
Thankfully, 2017's "Wonder Woman" bucked this&nbsp;
trend by offering moviegoers an engaging,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:38.760
visually interesting superhero story that critics&nbsp;
and general audiences alike would come to agree&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.800
was a triumph for the genre. For a moment, it&nbsp;
seemed like the DCEU was on the right track.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.900
But Warner Bros. failed to maintain consistent&nbsp;
quality across their DC releases post-"Wonder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.460
Woman," and with the sequel, the "Wonder Woman"&nbsp;
series also ran into the issue of quality control.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.840
In 2020, director Patty Jenkins&nbsp;
and Diana Prince actress Gal Gadot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:03.180
reunited for "Wonder Woman 1984," a period&nbsp;
piece focused on the Amazonian princess set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.620
in the '80s that calls back to the Richard&nbsp;
Donner "Superman" era of comic book films.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:11.520
Sadly, unlike its predecessor, it&nbsp;
struggled tremendously to win folks over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.120
as evidenced by numerous poor&nbsp;
reviews and a muted fan reaction.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:19.260
Even though "Wonder Woman 1984" wound&nbsp;
up becoming something of a misfire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:24.120
Warner Bros. at one point still planned to get&nbsp;
the ball rolling on "Wonder Woman 3." Sadly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:28.320
for those hoping to see the "Wonder Woman"&nbsp;
trilogy completed, plans have since changed.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:33.300
As revealed on December 7, 2022 by The&nbsp;
Hollywood Reporter, "Wonder Woman 3" is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:37.020
officially off the table at Warner Bros.&nbsp;
Discovery. According to the publication,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.880
Patty Jenkins recently submitted a treatment she&nbsp;
put together alongside co-writer Geoff Johns,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:45.540
only for them to find out that the feature&nbsp;
is no longer on DC's release slate.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:49.980
The reason for this move? DC Studios&nbsp;
heads James Gunn and Peter Safran,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:53.460
as well as Warner Bros. Pictures'&nbsp;
Michael De Luca and Pamela Abdy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.180
who all reportedly felt the threequel wouldn't&nbsp;
fit within the studio's new direction.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:02.280
This announcement comes shortly after Gunn&nbsp;
and Safran were selected to helm DC Studios,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:05.400
in hopes of keeping DC-related&nbsp;
films and television programs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.834
cohesive and of the highest quality possible.

00:02:07.834 --> 00:02:09.960
At the time the THR report was published,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:15.240
the duo was set to meet with Warner Bros.&nbsp;
Discovery CEO David Zaslav to work out the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:18.600
specifics of what the DC Universe will&nbsp;
look like under their watchful eyes.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:23.400
"Wonder Woman 3" now joins the likes of&nbsp;
fellow 2022 cancellations "Batgirl" and "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:27.540
Wonder Twins" in the DC media graveyard,&nbsp;
while such productions as "Shazam! Fury&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.320
of the Gods," the ever-controversial&nbsp;
"The Flash," and more remain intact.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:36.180
According to a Deadline report about new DC&nbsp;
heads James Gunn and Peter Safran canceling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:40.560
"Wonder Woman 3," one anonymous source claimed&nbsp;
that the door is open for director Patty Jenkins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.820
to submit plans for an entirely new "Wonder&nbsp;
Woman" project, despite the cancellation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:49.380
her threequel. Seemingly, then, Gunn and Safran&nbsp;
have no issue with Jenkins' work as a filmmaker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:53.640
so much as they genuinely seem to be taking&nbsp;
the DC film universe in a brand new direction.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:58.980
Gal Gadot's future with DC, meanwhile, is&nbsp;
murkier. On December 6, just prior to news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:03.180
of the "Wonder Woman" cancellation, Gadot&nbsp;
tweeted about her longtime superhero role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:06.960
concluding with the promise that she "Can't&nbsp;
wait to share [Diana's] next chapter with you."

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.160
But that message came before the news broke that&nbsp;
the planned sequel was no longer moving forward.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.720
Whether or not Gadot might remain a part of&nbsp;
any future Jenkins "Wonder Woman" project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.760
or even a part the DC cinematic universe moving&nbsp;
forward, is not quite certain for the time being.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.880
Perhaps someday we'll see Patty&nbsp;
Jenkins and Gal Gadot's "Wonder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.820
Woman" trilogy completed,&nbsp;
but for now it's in the bin.

